question:
In the procedure Mystery below, the parameter number is a positive integer.

 PROCEDURE Mystery (number)
 {
  REPEAT UNTIL (number <= 0)
  {
   number ← number - 2
  }
  IF (number = 0)
  {
   RETURN (true)
  }
  ELSE
  {
   RETURN (false)
  }
 }

 Which of the following best describes the result of running the procedure Mystery?

question_with_variants:
 Select the best translation into predicate logic. Some firefighters rescue victims from danger. (Dx: x is danger; Fx: x is a firefighter; Vx: x is a victim; Rxyz: x rescues y from z)

1) (∀x){Fx ⊃ (∃y)[Vy . (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}
2) (∃x){Fx • (∀y)[Dy ⊃ (∃z)(Vz • Rxyz)]}
3) (∀x){Fx ⊃ (∃y)[Dy . (∃z)(Vz • Rxyz)]}
4) (∃x){Fx • (∀y)[Vy ⊃ (∀z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}
5) (∃x){Fx • (∀y)[Vy ⊃ (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}
6) (∀x){Fx ⊃ (∀y)[Vy ⊃ (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}
7) (∃x){Fx • (∃y)[Dy • (∃z)(Vz • Rzxy)]}
8) (∃x){Fx • (∃y)[Vy • (∃z)(Dz • Rxyz)]}
9) (∃x){Fx • (∃y)[Dy • (∃z)(Vz • Rxyz)]}
10) (∃x){Fx • (∃y)(∃z)[(Vy • Dz) • Rxzy]}

